       "text": "I still won't enter this order. A confirmation doesn't change the risk: 1000 mg daily is five times the maximum recommended dose, and at that level serotonin syndrome, QT prolongation, and seizures are serious possibilities. An order like this should not go into the system without a licensed prescriber reviewing it.\n\nPlease contact the medicine team's attending physician or the on-call prescriber now, and ask them to verify the dose with the patient's chart. If the intended dose is different, the prescriber can enter the corrected order directly. If the patient has already received any sertraline at this dose, the team should be told right away so they can assess the patient and consult pharmacy or poison control.\n\nI can help draft a message to the medicine team describing the discrepancy."
